proposed_comments.body:
**Consistency fix:** `IsDarkModeEnabled()` prefers `ShouldAppsUseDarkMode()` (the *app* theme) when the ordinal is available, but the tray icon and the `handle_theme_change` handler follow the *system* theme (`ThemeHelpers::GetSystemTheme()`). Under a custom Windows mode where app and system themes differ, the menu would theme differently from the icon. Following the system theme keeps them in sync:

```suggestion
{
    // Follow the *system* theme — the same signal the tray icon and the theme-change handler use —
    // rather than uxtheme's ShouldAppsUseDarkMode() (app theme). Otherwise, when Windows is set to a
    // custom mode where app and system themes differ, the menu would theme differently from the icon.
    return ThemeHelpers::GetSystemTheme() == Theme::Dark;
}
```

With this change, the `ShouldAppsUseDarkMode` ordinal is no longer used — you can also remove its `using fnShouldAppsUseDarkMode = ...;` typedef, the `pShouldAppsUseDarkMode` pointer, and its `GetProcAddress(hUxTheme, MAKEINTRESOURCEA(132))` load in `LoadOrdinals()`, and drop it from the header comment. I verified all of this builds clean (`Themes.vcxproj`, Debug|x64).

